## Measure CI time

Budget for job `ci`: 45 s on a typical PR, 15 s docs-only. Measure the last 20 runs:

```bash
gh run list -w ci.yml -L 20 --json databaseId
gh run view <id> --json jobs   # completedAt - startedAt of job "ci"
```

Ignore cancelled and skipped runs. The job summary of each run also shows its duration.

## PR previews

`preview.yml` builds apps on every PR with no secrets; `preview-deploy.yml` (environment `preview`)
uploads the result as version `pr-<n>` of `<app>-preview`. Store `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and
`CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` only as secrets of the `preview` environment (and of the prod deploy
environment), with Deployment branches set to Selected, `main`; never as repository secrets, which
every PR workflow could read.

## Update bot

`splice.yml` runs the weekly `splice update` on GitHub in every CI mode. Create the environment
`splice-bot` first (Deployment branches = Selected, `main`); a first run would auto-create an
unprotected one. Store its credentials only as secrets of that environment, never as repository
secrets: any pull request that edits a workflow could read those.

The bot also refreshes `pnpm-lock.yaml` (lockfile only, no install scripts) so catalog bumps
pass `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. splice skips that step when a merge conflicts: after
resolving the conflict PR, run `pnpm install --lockfile-only` and push.

### Update bot: pick a token mode

A PR opened with `github.token` gets no CI (events by `GITHUB_TOKEN` trigger no workflows), cannot
push changes to `.github/workflows/*` (needs the `workflows` permission), and so cannot merge when
a ruleset requires `ci-ok`. Pick one:

1. GitHub App (no personal token): install an App with Contents, Pull requests and Workflows write
   (required: `splice.yml` requests it, and the token step fails without it). In environment
   `splice-bot`, set the variable `SPLICE_APP_CLIENT_ID` (the App's Client ID) and the secret
   `SPLICE_APP_KEY` (its private key).
2. PAT: `SPLICE_BOT_TOKEN` as an environment secret (Contents, Pull requests and Workflows write).
3. Session mode: set the repository variable `SPLICE_BOT=off`. The job is skipped (scheduled and
   manual runs); an agent session runs `splice update --all` on a branch and opens the PR itself.
   Its push is not by `GITHUB_TOKEN`, so CI runs; pushing changes to workflow files needs a
   credential with the workflow scope.

Order: App, then PAT, then `github.token`.
